-- title:
--   ℓ≠ p: the second Hecke leg preserves crossing points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$, and let $K\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field `x1FunctionField (M * p)` of $X_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $j\in K$ have Laurent expansion the image of `jq`. Let $\ell$ be a prime and let $K_\ell$ be the analogous $L$-subfield attached to `x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p) (M * p * ℓ)`, the $q$-expansion field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)\cap\Gamma_0(Mp\ell)$, with $j_\ell\in K_\ell$ again expanding to `jq`; assume `HeckeBetaOneDefined (M * p) ℓ`, i.e. $q\mapsto q^\ell$ carries the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ into that of $\Gamma_1(Mp)\cap\Gamma_0(Mp\ell)$. Let $\pi_\alpha,\pi_\beta$ be finite, topologically surjective morphisms over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ from the two-chart model `modelTo A K_ℓ jℓ` to `modelTo A K j`, induced on the finite charts by $A$-algebra maps $\iota_\alpha,\iota_\beta\colon$ `chartAlgFin A K j` $\to$ `chartAlgFin A K_ℓ jℓ` that on Laurent series are, respectively, the identity and `qExpand L ℓ` (substitution $q\mapsto q^\ell$), the compatibilities being the two stated commuting squares with the chart immersions `ιFin`. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and an $A$-algebra, and let $i_1\colon C_1$, $i_2\colon C_2$ be closed immersions into the base change of `modelTo A K j` along $A\to k$ of two proper, smooth of relative dimension one, geometrically integral $k$-curves, whose images together cover every point of that base change. Let $\pi_{\alpha,k},\pi_{\beta,k}$ be morphisms of the $k$-fibres compatible with $\pi_\alpha,\pi_\beta$ and with the projections to $\operatorname{Spec} k$, and assume $\ell\neq p$. Then for every point $z$ of the $k$-fibre of `modelTo A K_ℓ jℓ`, if $\pi_{\alpha,k}(z)$ lies in the intersection of the images of $i_1$ and $i_2$, so does $\pi_{\beta,k}(z)$.
--
--   The assertion is set-theoretic, on underlying topological spaces: the crossing locus of the mod $p$ fibre of $X_1(Mp)$ consists of the supersingular points, and an $\ell$-isogeny with $\ell\neq p$ preserves supersingularity, so the two degeneracy legs of the Hecke correspondence at $\ell$ agree as to which points of the $\ell$-level fibre sit over crossings. It is used in the construction of a factorisation of Hecke data across the crossing points of the special fibre, in the level-lowering analysis of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$.
